00:05:11.150 --> 00:05:12.930
Of course not.

00:05:16.270 --> 00:05:16.510
Okay.

00:05:17.430 --> 00:05:23.510
I'll see that Mr. Canepa gets a check and a letter congratulating him on his choice of attorneys.

00:05:24.070 --> 00:05:24.430
Thank you.

00:05:27.870 --> 00:05:29.450
Do you always attend to these matters?

00:05:30.350 --> 00:05:31.530
Personally, Mr. Regan.

00:05:31.760 --> 00:05:33.840
Well, I thought my client was getting pushed around.

00:05:35.380 --> 00:05:36.080
I didn't like that.

00:05:37.830 --> 00:05:39.060
Well, goodbye, Mr. Corbin.

00:05:39.420 --> 00:05:39.660
Goodbye.

00:05:41.340 --> 00:05:42.560
Sorry if I got you in a jam.

00:05:43.340 --> 00:05:44.620
Anything for the cause of justice.

00:05:47.160 --> 00:05:49.580
Say, you know, you're a lot prettier than the girls out there.

00:05:49.700 --> 00:05:52.950
But obviously, that's why you're in here.

00:05:53.360 --> 00:05:53.760
Obviously.

00:05:55.030 --> 00:05:57.290
What do you do Saturday nights?

00:05:58.260 --> 00:05:59.790
Oh, play marbles.

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:11.020
girls next door. Look, I know of a little place. I'm sure you do. Well, the name's Regan, Robert

00:06:11.020 --> 00:06:19.260
Regan. I'll try to remember. I'm in the book in case your push card ever gets pushed. It very rarely

00:06:19.260 --> 00:06:25.800
does. I don't anticipate any serious trouble on this loan, Andrew. Did you ring Mr. Colby? Oh,

00:06:26.020 --> 00:06:29.830
yes, Miss Faraday. Did Mr. Murdoch return? No, he hasn't. It is unfortunate.

00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:33.040
that Krona should be getting out of prison at precisely this time.

00:06:33.240 --> 00:06:37.820
You can assure everyone concerned that Krona has absolutely no connection with my organization any longer.

00:06:37.940 --> 00:06:39.500
I think that's all we need. Goodbye.

00:06:39.800 --> 00:06:40.060
Goodbye.

00:06:41.380 --> 00:06:42.980
I'm sorry about the interruption, Andrew.

00:06:43.420 --> 00:06:44.220
You mean Regan?

00:06:44.900 --> 00:06:46.460
