Looks like you guessed right. We picked up the boy and girl at the station.

01:15:19.990 --> 01:15:22.570
I hope you'll be able to get this over with as quickly as possible.

01:15:22.670 --> 01:15:23.790
I'm not anxious to hang around.

01:15:31.400 --> 01:15:32.520
Regan, that was Charles.

01:15:33.380 --> 01:15:34.260
was his right.

01:15:34.980 --> 01:15:37.060
You may as well relax D'Amico accordingly when he wants you.

01:15:39.240 --> 01:15:39.700
What have I been doing?

01:15:46.730 --> 01:15:47.610
Why are they holding us?

01:15:49.160 --> 01:15:50.760
Because I'm the biggest lunkhead of the year?

01:15:51.340 --> 01:15:52.960
It never occurred to me he'd take it out on you.

01:15:53.700 --> 01:15:54.040
Andrew?

01:15:54.440 --> 01:15:55.580
No lame brain, our Andrew.

01:15:56.490 --> 01:15:59.750
He's gotten rid of the last guy to do anything about the phony bond deal and he stuck us with.

01:16:00.000 --> 01:16:00.240
map.

01:16:00.440 --> 01:16:00.680
Mm-hmm.

01:16:01.880 --> 01:16:04.180
walking around in the clouds, this guy blows a hole under me.

01:16:05.460 --> 01:16:05.820
couldn't.

01:16:06.390 --> 01:16:07.770
Possibly hope to get away with this.

01:16:09.910 --> 01:16:11.190
Why would we want to kill Charles?

01:16:11.420 --> 01:16:14.300
Don't worry. With Colby tailoring the evidence, it'll fit like a bathing suit.

01:16:16.700 --> 01:16:17.580
I figured you were in with me.

01:16:23.380 --> 01:16:26.560
If I could get loose for five minutes, I'd kick myself around the block.

01:16:28.120 --> 01:16:28.840
All right, you two.

01:16:29.340 --> 01:16:29.940
D'Amico's ready.

01:16:30.000 --> 01:16:30.340
for you now.

01:16:34.340 --> 01:16:34.660
Come along.

01:16:49.260 --> 01:16:49.860
little lady's fingerprints.

01:16:54.540 --> 01:16:56.780
Well, Laughing Boy, I thought I told you not to leave town.

01:16:57.320 --> 01:16:58.040
Get out, D'Amico.

01:16:58.600 --> 01:16:59.440
What are the details?

01:17:00.000 --> 01:17:01.260
Murder and grand theft.

01:17:02.260 --> 01:17:04.180
And you have an assured prayer of getting out of it.

01:17:06.300 --> 01:17:07.220
How does she figure in?

01:17:09.300 --> 01:17:10.920
Come now, Regan, let's not be ridiculous.

01:17:13.460 --> 01:17:14.100
Did you find the money?

01:17:14.940 --> 01:17:15.640
She had it on her.

01:17:15.900 --> 01:17:17.580
She was buying two tickets to Mexico City.

01:17:19.990 --> 01:17:21.450
Suppose she wanted a change of scenery.

01:17:24.790 --> 01:17:26.230
You want to identify this, Mr. Colby?

01:17:27.480 --> 01:17:28.560
Yes, that's the envelope.

01:17:30.030 --> 01:17:31.910
I assume the $10,000 is the same.

01:17:32.130 --> 01:17:36.690
Get me a stenographer in here.

01:17:37.220 --> 01:17:37.940
He's right here, Lieutenant.

01:17:38.510 --> 01:17:38.790
Fine.

01:17:38.930 --> 01:17:43.570
Got anything to say yet, Regan?

01:17:45.030 --> 01:17:46.430
I'm speechless with your efficiency.

01:17:46.810 --> 01:17:55.160
Let's have it, Mr. Colby.

01:17:55.240 --> 01:17:59.400
You understand that this is very difficult for me.

01:18:00.660 --> 01:18:03.160
Miss Faraday has been my secretary for over six years.

01:18:04.630 --> 01:18:06.250
Her father was one of my dearest friends.

01:18:07.100 --> 01:18:07.580
I understand.

01:18:08.860 --> 01:18:09.480
Well, I...

01:18:10.300 --> 01:18:13.640
I was up in my room doing some work about an hour ago.

01:18:15.160 --> 01:18:15.980
And I heard a shot.

01:18:17.590 --> 01:18:18.990
At first, I thought it was my imagination.

01:18:20.690 --> 01:18:21.070
then I

01:18:21.500 --> 01:18:22.400
I decided to investigate.

01:18:23.740 --> 01:18:24.780
I found Charles.

01:18:25.050 --> 01:18:25.990
dead on the floor.

01:18:27.320 --> 01:18:27.560
Good.

01:18:27.830 --> 01:18:29.250
Regan's gun beside him.

01:18:30.730 --> 01:18:31.690
the safe was open.

01:18:32.010 --> 01:18:33.550
But D'Amico, that was his gun.

01:18:33.670 --> 01:18:35.470
You can't keep quiet. We'll do this without you.

01:18:35.550 --> 01:18:37.090
I gave it back to him two days ago.

01:18:37.150 --> 01:18:37.770
Who saw you?

01:18:37.850 --> 01:18:38.690
Miss Faraday, she...

01:18:38.690 --> 01:18:39.090
Mm-hmm.

01:18:44.040 --> 01:18:44.960
Go ahead, Mr. Colby.

01:18:45.220 --> 01:18:49.320
Well, I realized that Miss Faraday was the only person besides Charles and myself

01:18:49.320 --> 01:18:51.260
who knew the combination to the same.

01:18:51.530 --> 01:18:53.270
Andrew, you had me open this safe yourself.

01:18:54.220 --> 01:18:58.860
A couple of nights ago, I happened to overhear a conversation between Mr. Regan and...

01:18:58.950 --> 01:18:59.790
Miss Faraday.

01:19:00.000 --> 01:19:00.340
which

01:19:01.180 --> 01:19:02.700
Mexico City was mentioned.

01:19:03.800 --> 01:19:05.340
When I called the police, I...

01:19:05.400 --> 01:19:06.080
told them that.

01:19:07.160 --> 01:19:07.840
Okay, thanks.

01:19:08.180 --> 01:19:10.620
She was buying two tickets to Mexico City when we picked them up.

01:19:10.720 --> 01:19:11.620
You already told me that.

01:19:12.540 --> 01:19:13.600
What are you looking for, a promotion?

01:19:14.620 --> 01:19:16.920
Lieutenant, he knows why I had the money. He sent me for the tickets.

01:19:17.080 --> 01:19:18.960
You'll get your chance to talk later, Miss Faraday.

01:19:23.320 --> 01:19:24.420
What are you trying to do, Andrew?

01:19:26.040 --> 01:19:28.080
Everyone that's ever meant anything to you.

01:19:29.370 --> 01:19:29.830
Kroner?

01:19:30.790 --> 01:19:31.330
Charles?

01:19:32.650 --> 01:19:33.330
And now me.

01:19:34.200 --> 01:19:36.000
Lieutenant, this is very awkward for me.

01:19:36.060 --> 01:19:36.940
We're nearly finished, Mr.

01:19:37.000 --> 01:19:39.340
Why do you believe him, D'Amico? Only yesterday.

01:19:39.340 --> 01:19:40.000
That was yesterday.

01:19:41.060 --> 01:19:42.660
I'm not interested in that case anymore.

01:19:42.760 --> 01:19:45.220
Personally, I got one right here that suits me fine.

01:19:45.400 --> 01:19:45.600
Look.

01:19:46.020 --> 01:19:47.700
What do you want, the truth or a quick arrest?

01:19:47.800 --> 01:19:48.480
What's your story?

01:19:49.000 --> 01:19:49.800
This is a frame.

01:19:50.700 --> 01:19:52.860
You get framed more than any guy I ever met.

01:19:53.540 --> 01:19:55.500
You're supposed to be a lawyer. Take a look at the evidence.

01:19:55.980 --> 01:19:56.580
Oh, D'Amico.

01:19:58.540 --> 01:19:59.580
You'd better change your charge.

01:20:00.000 --> 01:20:01.100
The corpse is still alive.

01:20:01.500 --> 01:20:01.900
Alarm!

01:20:03.190 --> 01:20:06.390
We won't have them forever, but I may be able to string them along through the night.

01:20:07.510 --> 01:20:08.590
Any chance of him coming too?

01:20:09.460 --> 01:20:10.520
If we don't move him.

01:20:11.930 --> 01:20:13.070
Let me know the minute he comes around.

01:20:14.230 --> 01:20:15.870
Is it all right if we leave him here, Mr. Colby?

01:20:15.990 --> 01:20:16.370
Of course.

01:20:17.240 --> 01:20:18.640
Charles is my very dear friend.

01:20:18.940 --> 01:20:20.400
I'll see about having him moved upstairs.

01:20:20.860 --> 01:20:21.720
Don't let him near that room.

01:20:21.780 --> 01:20:22.800
Are you still running this case?

01:20:24.180 --> 01:20:25.980
I'm telling you, D'Amico, don't let this guy near us.

01:20:26.060 --> 01:20:26.820
Just a minute, Regan.

01:20:27.640 --> 01:20:29.860
You're under arrest. You're not giving any advice around here.

01:20:30.000 --> 01:20:30.800
That's where you're headed.

01:20:31.020 --> 01:20:33.000
He's been one of my closest friends for years, naturally.

01:20:33.160 --> 01:20:34.340
I'd want to see him before he dies.

01:20:34.600 --> 01:20:35.580
The doctor says he can't be moved.

01:20:36.490 --> 01:20:39.390
With him liable to pop off any minute, I'd better wait around and have a talk with him.

01:20:41.060 --> 01:20:42.480
Maybe we all better wait around.

01:21:00.000 --> 01:21:00.980
Thank you.

01:21:19.190 --> 01:21:19.590
suspect.

01:22:08.980 --> 01:22:09.380
Regan.

01:22:09.780 --> 01:22:09.980
You

01:22:11.990 --> 01:22:13.410
Why couldn't we tell them about Bruno?

01:22:15.260 --> 01:22:17.020
How do you think that would sound from the witness stand?

01:22:18.580 --> 01:22:23.400
I was trying to find a man named Victor Bruno because I was convinced that the other killing I'd done...

01:22:23.510 --> 01:22:24.050
was murder.

01:22:27.540 --> 01:22:28.280
figured on that one.

01:22:30.440 --> 01:22:31.940
If only somebody could find it.

01:22:32.620 --> 01:22:33.800
Broome was probably dead too.

01:22:34.790 --> 01:22:37.030
Otherwise, how could Colby be sure it wasn't Bruno on the phone?

01:22:38.340 --> 01:22:38.700
So

01:22:41.100 --> 01:22:42.360
How could I be such a dope?

01:22:42.980 --> 01:22:43.240
Yo.

01:22:45.670 --> 01:22:47.150
I've been second-guessing the whole way.

01:22:48.650 --> 01:22:49.950
Regan, the boy detective.

01:22:52.130 --> 01:22:53.610
Couldn't have put your life in worse hands.

01:22:56.580 --> 01:22:57.220
Come on in, Regan.

01:22:57.770 --> 01:22:58.790
I want to ask you a couple of questions.

01:23:00.980 --> 01:23:01.780
What about Charles?

01:23:02.260 --> 01:23:03.100
He's still out.

01:25:00.000 --> 01:25:00.940
since you shot him.

01:25:11.420 --> 01:25:12.000
knock them down.

01:25:13.140 --> 01:25:13.680
Pick him up.

01:25:20.470 --> 01:25:21.550
Tough break, Mr. Colby.

01:25:22.520 --> 01:25:24.180
I really solved this one from left field.

01:25:25.270 --> 01:25:27.170
I've had Regan tail for the last three days.

01:25:28.310 --> 01:25:29.370
I knew he wasn't here tonight.

01:25:30.090 --> 01:25:34.270
Quite a comfort to us taxpayers to find our police department in such competent hands.

01:25:34.630 --> 01:25:35.910
Thanks. Thanks so much.

01:25:36.940 --> 01:25:37.700
Oh, uh...

01:25:37.800 --> 01:25:38.300
personally

01:25:38.660 --> 01:25:39.800
just to keep the record straight.

01:25:40.490 --> 01:25:42.190
Whatever happened to Kroner's million bucks?

01:25:43.140 --> 01:25:43.680
That's funny.

01:25:44.740 --> 01:25:46.220
That's what Croner wanted to know.

01:25:47.340 --> 01:25:47.680
Yeah!

01:25:48.780 --> 01:25:49.520
Very funny.

01:25:51.040 --> 01:25:51.620
Wait a minute.

01:25:52.230 --> 01:25:53.170
What do you think you're doing?

01:25:53.740 --> 01:25:55.580
He still owes my client $68.

01:25:56.550 --> 01:25:57.770
And 72 cents.

01:25:58.600 --> 01:25:59.420
Well, you're a lawyer.

01:26:00.280 --> 01:26:00.720
Sue him.

01:26:10.960 --> 01:26:13.380
That D'Amico is really the answer to a maiden's prayer.

01:26:13.700 --> 01:26:14.160
You're right.

01:26:14.450 --> 01:26:15.510
He's a smart cookie.

01:26:16.240 --> 01:26:16.400
Huh?

01:26:16.500 --> 01:26:18.160
He doesn't catch everything.

01:26:19.020 --> 01:26:19.460
What's that?

01:26:20.420 --> 01:26:21.980
Tickets to Mexico City.

01:26:26.440 --> 01:26:27.260
Oh, forget you two.

01:26:27.340 --> 01:26:29.840
You'll have to check with my department if you're figuring out leaving the country.

01:26:30.220 --> 01:26:30.640
Thank you.
